(piecewise linear)Definition: {The Linear Interpolation function takes two vectors X and Y having along the same index I.  Given a target value V between two points on X, the function returns a linearly inerpolated value between two points on Y.~
In this example, X and Y are Volume Thresholds and Cost Points, respectively. V is the total ingredient quantity.  The function returns total cost for each ingredient.~
Syntax is LinearInterp(X,Y,V,I)}~
LinearInterp(Volume_Thresholds, Cost_Points, Ingredient_qty, Price_Point_Index)NodeLocation: 400,392,1NodeSize: 72,32ValueState: 2,667,23,327,247,0,MIDMVariable Cost_PointsTitle: Cost PointsDefinition: Cumulate(Ingredient_Prices*Volume_Increments,Price_Point_Index)NodeLocation: 992,160,1NodeSize: 48,24ValueState: 2,32,43,443,303,0,MIDMReformVal: [Price_Point_Index,Ingredient]Module Exhaustive_SearchTitle: Exhaustive SearchAuthor: PaulDate: Mon, Apr 11, 2011 1:13 PMDefaultSize: 48,24NodeLocation: 112,384,1NodeSize: 48,24NodeInfo: 1,0,1,1,1,1,0,,0,DiagState: 2,-7,0,827,432,17Index Permutation_indexTitle: Permutation indexDefinition: 1..5^4NodeLocation: 96,52,1NodeSize: 48,24ValueState: 2,19,111,284,303,0,MIDMVariable Permutations1Title: PermutationsDefinition: mod(Floor((Permutation_index-1)/5^(4-@Cereal)),5)+1NodeLocation: 240,56,1NodeSize: 56,28DefnState: 2,137,174,590,303,0,MIDMValueState: 2,32,43,685,303,0,MIDMReformDef: [Cereal,Permutation_index]ReformVal: [Cereal,Permutation_index]Variable Cost_for_all_permutaTitle: Cost for all permutationsDefinition: var quantity := Sum(Production_Qty*Cereal_Recipes[Recipe_Index = Permutations1]/100, Cereal);~
